From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: <your git identity>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] csvsplit: fix heap-buffer-overflow in copy_quoted()

In copy_quoted(), line 22 allocates `inner` bytes (n-2) for the unquoted
content but does not reserve space for the terminating NUL.
AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow at src/csvsplit.c:33.
---
 src/csvsplit.c | 2 +-
 1 file(s) changed, 1 insertion(s)(+), 1 deletion(s)(-)

diff --git a/src/csvsplit.c b/src/csvsplit.c
--- a/src/csvsplit.c
+++ b/src/csvsplit.c
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
  * quote, `n` counts every byte up to and including the closing quote. */
 static char *copy_quoted(const char *raw, size_t n) {
     size_t inner = n >= 2 ? n - 2 : 0;
-    char *field = malloc(inner); /* room for the content */
+    char *field = malloc(inner + 1); /* room for the content and NUL terminator */
     size_t out = 0;
     if (field == NULL) {
         return NULL;
--
leakproof package
